@startuml
title Morning Briefing Backend and Production Package Architecture
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
left to right direction

actor Browser
cloud "Shared ALB\nTLS + AWS WAF" as SharedAlb
node "Consolidated ARM64 EC2\npersonal-projects" as Host {
  component "Release activator\nuser-owned staging bundle\nSHA-256 + manifest verified\nsudo -n root boundary" as ReleaseActivator
  component "Apache 2.4\n:8080" as Apache
  package "Morning Briefing Compose Release" as Compose {
    component "Frontend\nStrict TypeScript + Vite 8\nNginx static SPA\nloopback port" as Frontend
    package "Backend image\nNode.js + Fastify" as BackendImage {
      component "Backend API\n/api/v1 + DB/broker readiness" as Backend
      component "Worker\nmanual ack + bounded prefetch" as Worker
      component "One-shot commands\nmigrate / widget refresh / audio refresh" as OneShots
    }
    folder "Persistent audio\nAUDIO_BRIEFING_STORAGE_DIR" as AudioStorage
    queue "RabbitMQ\ndurable quorum queues" as Rabbit
    folder "Persistent RabbitMQ data" as RabbitStorage
  }
  component "systemd timers\n01:00 / 05:00 UTC\nRoot-owned oneshot boundary\nPersistent + locked / umask 0077" as Timers
}

package "Backend modular monolith" as ModularBackend {
  package "API Layer" as ApiLayer {
    [Routes]
    [Schemas]
    [Auth Middleware]
  }
  package "Application Layer" as AppLayer {
    [Dashboard Use Cases]
    [User Profile Use Cases]
    [Widget Use Cases]
    [Connector Use Cases]
    [Briefing Use Cases]
    [Audio Briefing Use Cases]
  }
  package "Domain Layer" as DomainLayer {
    [Dashboard Domain]
    [Widget Domain]
    [Connector Domain]
    [Snapshot Domain]
  }
  package "Infrastructure Layer" as InfraLayer {
    [Prisma Repositories]
    [Connector Clients]
    [Confirmed Job Publisher]
    [Snapshot Job Processor]
    [LLM Provider]
    [TTS Provider]
    [Delivery Channels]
    [Observability]
  }
}

database "PostgreSQL 18.4\nexternal Docker network\npersonal-projects-postgresql" as Postgres
queue "Main quorum queue\ndurable job deliveries" as MainQueue
queue "Retry quorum queue\nTTL backoff" as RetryQueue
queue "Terminal quorum DLQ" as Dlq
cloud "Life2 Auth\nsign-in + JWT callback" as AuthService
folder "Root-owned env files\noutside releases / mode 0600" as Secrets
cloud "CloudWatch Logs\nawslogs / 7-day retention" as CloudWatch
cloud "External providers\nGoogle / weather / RSS / tasks" as Providers
cloud "OpenAI Responses API" as OpenAi
cloud "AWS Polly" as Polly
cloud "Telegram Bot API" as Telegram
cloud "SMTP / Amazon SES" as Mail

Browser --> SharedAlb : HTTPS briefing.ralfepoisson.com
ReleaseActivator --> Compose : atomically install immutable release
SharedAlb --> Apache : HTTP :8080
Apache --> Backend : /api/*
Apache --> Frontend : all other paths
Frontend --> Backend : REST /api/v1
Frontend --> AuthService : sign-in redirect
AuthService --> Frontend : /#/auth/callback + JWT

Backend ..> ApiLayer
Worker ..> [Snapshot Job Processor]
OneShots ..> AppLayer
ApiLayer --> AppLayer
AppLayer --> DomainLayer
AppLayer --> InfraLayer
[Prisma Repositories] --> Postgres
[Confirmed Job Publisher] --> Rabbit : persistent + mandatory\npublisher confirms
Rabbit --> MainQueue
MainQueue --> Worker : at-least-once / manual ack
Worker --> RetryQueue : retryable failure
RetryQueue --> MainQueue : TTL expiry / backoff
Worker --> Dlq : bounded x-death exhausted\nor invalid envelope
Rabbit --> RabbitStorage : durable state
[Snapshot Job Processor] --> [Briefing Use Cases]
[Snapshot Job Processor] --> [Audio Briefing Use Cases]
[Connector Clients] --> Providers
[LLM Provider] --> OpenAi
[TTS Provider] --> Polly
[Delivery Channels] --> Telegram
[Delivery Channels] --> Mail
Backend --> Secrets : scoped runtime secrets
Worker --> Secrets : scoped runtime secrets
Backend --> AudioStorage : read/playback
Worker --> AudioStorage : generate/deliver
Timers --> OneShots : locked one-shot execution
Frontend --> CloudWatch : Docker awslogs
Backend --> CloudWatch : Docker awslogs
Worker --> CloudWatch : Docker awslogs
Rabbit --> CloudWatch : Docker awslogs

note on link
Host root reaches the protected release and Docker socket.
The one-shot container retains its non-root application UID;
runtime secret files remain root-owned mode 0600.
end note

note bottom of Host
Publisher transport cannot traverse /srv/apps as the login user.
Root copies and verifies the staged bundle before extraction.
Application containers do not own PostgreSQL.
Backend and frontend bind only to loopback-facing ports.
Backend, worker, and one-shots use a separate egress bridge
for AWS and provider APIs; PostgreSQL remains internal.
RabbitMQ is reachable only on the internal application network.
Worker and timers stay disabled until the approved
ECS/EventBridge writer handoff.
end note

note bottom of Postgres
The restored production database was verified at
19 public base tables and 92,767 rows.
Port 5432 is not publicly exposed.
end note

note bottom of Dlq
The broker provides durable delivery, retry backoff, and a
terminal DLQ. PostgreSQL job rows remain authoritative for
idempotency, leases, attempt evidence, and stale-job decisions.
end note

note bottom of Secrets
Includes DATABASE_URL, MESSAGE_BROKER_URL,
RabbitMQ bootstrap credentials, OAuth/JWT/delivery secrets,
and OPENAI_API_KEY. No secret is stored in a release or image.
end note

note bottom of SharedAlb
The legacy ECS/Fargate ALB and drifted CloudFormation stack
remain rollback surfaces until separately approved retirement.
end note

@enduml
